// expect: 10
// A generic constructor's payload widths are the instantiation's, so a
// pattern under a Float twin finds the second payload after an 8-byte first
// one. The payload types the pattern carries are the body's own variables,
// and the offset fold read them without the twin's instantiation, as words.
// Measured on boot 0bc8383e: 3 — `second(Pair(1.5, 7))` read half of 1.5.
type P = Pair(a, b)

fn second(p) = match p {
  Pair(_, y) => y,
}

fn main() = second(Pair(1.5, 7)) + second(Pair(2, 3))
